[Music]  for me  the big picture is really trying to  you know understand the things that are  going to be meaningful to my friends  to my family to my children when i'm  gone  playing with my kids or telling them a  story  i think it's just a reminder that it  matters because it's really hard to do  those little things  sometimes when you're not feeling it and  as a parent  you're usually not feeling it and so our  vision was to create a simple  beautiful baby brand to help moms  make their lives easier at first this  for several years we were just hustling  i mean we were just  working hard i was up late we were  receiving pallets to our house  it was just time after time after time  people would ask me questions  i had no idea and it felt like it was a  year  before i was asked a question that i  knew the answer to  [Music]  so i was at basis scottsdale for a  couple years teaching  and then i moved to a christian school  and i was running their missions program  during that time is when we started our  business lucy darling  so in the winter of 2012 my wife had  this idea  when she had when she was pregnant for  our daughter wanted to create a really  beautiful  product that would be helpful for us to  remember how old she was as she was  growing  a little sticker to put on her onesie  as she was getting older month by month  she said  actually because i can't find anything  maybe there's a hole in the market  that's something that we could do and  she said but we'd need to invest a  little bit of money and i thought  how much money are we talking about here  and she said a hundred dollars  i mean this is this is really going to  cut out of that teacher salary  so it was a three-day conversation about  this this seed money investment of 100  u.s dollars and i said all right i trust  you  let's let's put all the money in and so  we did we put all the 100  in and yeah i guess we haven't looked  back  [Music]  you know a lot of students have this  grand vision of  what they're going to accomplish once  they graduate from college  that was not my story my story was i  didn't really know what i wanted to do  as i finished high school my economics  teacher from my high school took us down  i can't even i think it was a lecture  from dr wolfram  and while i was on campus i was walking  by  the library and out walked clarence  thomas  that was pretty cool and so seeing him i  was like  huh i think i uh i should give a little  bit of thought to this place  and so at hillsdale immediately i just  fell in love with the place  it was maybe my junior year  but there was a restaurant there called  the saucy dog i don't know if it's still  there  but we had i think on tuesdays they had  25 cent wings night  and my roommate and i decided hey you  know what i bet we could afford to take  a professor out to dinner  you know what's he going to eat 12 wings  you know we had  tons of guys out for for this uh for  dinner  i know we had dr jackson and dr connor  and i think even  victor davis hansen came out life's hard  right there's all kinds of challenges  that we face you know  having kids is tough being married is  tough running a business is tough  and so you need to be bold enough to do  difficult things i was able to see at  hillsdale these wise men and women  who cared about me and were able to give  good counsel  so that as i've seen other challenges  challenges at work  jobs that i've had before challenges in  marriage challenges in raising  my children i've gone back to that  sort of habit that i've created which is  going to those that i that i know love  and care for me  and seeking their advice  [Music]  you know one of the the things that has  been really  helpful with our business is my wife is  very talented  she's very good at making beautiful  things and so  you know for me my goal and my job  basically from the beginning has been  how do we sell this  so at first we started the business on  etsy that's where we were doing all of  our business for the first year  and then we expanded to amazon that i  think that year  was full of a lot of challenges because  i had no idea what i was doing  i didn't know lingo i didn't know  process i didn't know anything and so i  had to figure it all out  on the fly while we were selling we  first  landed a deal with nordstrom we had i  had a hundred  page eight and a half by 11 pdf  that i had to read in order to  understand how to ship boxes to  nordstrom  and so these things were so overwhelming  at first  and we just had to plow through we were  receiving pallets to our house  on mondays we would get a pallet or two  or three delivered to the garage  and we would on that evening we would  bring everything inside and then we'd  have to label it and do all kinds of  stuff with it and then the next day  would be the pickup  and then we would have to have  everything palletized and it would be  pulled out of the garage and so it was  almost  three days a week was just that process  because we were getting bigger  and more orders i think when someone  asks you a question  you have no idea how to answer  especially when you're trying to  create a brand and a business it's it's  really humbling  because you're trying to figure out how  do i answer this correct question  correctly  but also not foolishly  since then we've been able to bring a  team together we have a warehouse and  fulfillment center  and so one of the things that's been  really neat is one  to be honest is just that my wife's a  very talented  designer it's been awesome to see  her strength working together  to to sort of give the world these  beautiful things that she has created  has been really satisfying

